        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-33" parent="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-36" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Le notifiche sono gestite come parte della business logic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Quando un admin aggiunge una issue e la assegna ad un utente si crea un nuovo record nella tabella Notification (utilizzando il pattern observer), si esponde l&#39;endpoint con l&#39;api con /notification ad esempio e si gestisce la notifica. La chiamata api può essere fatta ogni cambio di pagina, ogni lasso di tempo, quando si effettua log in, ect. Da vedere come bilanciare il numero di richieste api al tempo in cui l&#39;utente non visualizza ancora la propira notifica. Ovviamente va aggiunta la tabella al database.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="390" x="10" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-37" connectable="0" parent="1" style="group" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="600" x="980" y="3130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-31" parent="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-37" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="510" x="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-30" parent="TFcktgsDKx9lrRnR8x_w-37" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: start; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;controller&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Espone gli endpoint REST (&lt;code&gt;/issues&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/users&lt;/code&gt;, ecc.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;service&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Contiene &lt;strong&gt;tutta la logica applicativa&lt;/strong&gt; (validazioni, filtri, assegnazioni, ricerca)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;repository&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Isola l’accesso ai dati (Repository = DAO moderno)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Entity + enum di dominio (&lt;code&gt;Issue&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;User&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;IssueStatus&lt;/code&gt;, ecc.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dto&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Contratti API (input / output)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="600" y="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
